%% HAND-CURATED. Represents the 10-step middleware chain (sys-17 §3.1) — every inbound HTTP request passes through this exact order before reaching the route handler.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant Redis
    participant BackendService

    ParentApp->>Gateway: HTTP request (any /v1/* path)
    Gateway->>Gateway: step 1 — request-id — assign X-Request-Id if absent
    Gateway->>Redis: step 2 — ip-blocklist SISMEMBER ip_blocklist
    alt ip_blocked
        Redis-->>Gateway: member
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 403 IP_BLOCKED
    else clear
        Redis-->>Gateway: not-member
        Gateway->>Gateway: step 3 — cors — Origin allowlist check
        alt cors_denied
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 403 CORS_DENIED
        else allowed
            Gateway->>Gateway: step 4 — body-limit — reject oversized payload
            alt body_too_large
                Gateway-->>ParentApp: 413 PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE
            else within budget
                Gateway->>Gateway: step 5 — api-version — extract /v{N}/, set Sunset header if deprecated
                alt api_version_removed
                    Gateway-->>ParentApp: 410 Gone
                else supported
                    Gateway->>Gateway: step 6 — auth-resolver — route to JWT / mTLS / api_key / none by path
                    alt auth_failed
                        Note over Gateway: emit auth_failure event to SQS tbot-security-events (sys-13)
                        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 401 / 403
                    else authenticated
                        Gateway->>Redis: step 7 — rate-limiter — sliding-window Lua atomic check (see rate-limit-violation-event flow)
                        alt rate_limited
                            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 429 and Retry-After
                        else under limit
                            Gateway->>Gateway: step 8 — request-logger start — emit access-log start line
                            Gateway->>BackendService: dispatch to route handler
                            alt unhandled_internal_error
                                BackendService-->>Gateway: throws
                                Gateway->>Gateway: step 10 — error-formatter — shape to standard error envelope
                                Gateway->>Gateway: step 9 — request-logger complete — emit access-log with status
                                Gateway-->>ParentApp: 5xx standardized error
                            else success
                                BackendService-->>Gateway: handler response
                                Gateway->>Gateway: step 9 — request-logger complete — emit access-log with status
                                Gateway-->>ParentApp: 2xx response and rate-limit headers
                            end
                        end
                    end
                end
            end
        end
    end

    Note over ParentApp,BackendService: chain short-circuits on first reject — no middleware skipped — X-Request-Id propagates to all downstream services
